{"kind":"promise","text":"Claimed. I will survey the current web UI (ui/ views, routes, components) and the projection surfaces it reads (internal/statusview, GET /v0/status), then write one short plain-English design note under notes/ on branch request/ui-simplification-note. The note will carry: a screen inventory naming what is deleted and what survives, each survivor justified against \"what waits, and on whom?\"; a one-line row specification for a top-level list keyed on open requests (state, who it waits on, age); the ordering rule putting unclaimed and waiting-on-a-human work first; and a thread view reduced to the commitment spine with provenance hops, repair chains and chat behind explicit expansion. Deletion over configuration; no count without a click through to exactly the rows it counts. Composes with the staleness-presentation principle of 427b3bd3 and may assume the enriched row fields of c4d7ce8c. Design only: no runtime or source changes. I will publish an exact-head artifact at the note's path and request review from codex; ratification by hugh follows, and implementation is a separate request resting on the ratified decision."}